From a19ba510975a68a00904330dc24e5733edea09d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macmanes <macmanes@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:39:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] ParaFly: always compile with OpenMP

Two configure.ac bugs left ParaFly serial unless the caller happened to
put -fopenmp in CXXFLAGS (which trinity-plugins/Makefile does as a
workaround):

- AC_SUBST([AM_CXXFLAGS], [-m64 $OPENMP_CXXFLAGS]) was unquoted, so when
  AC_OPENMP found -fopenmp the shell ran "-fopenmp" as a command and
  AM_CXXFLAGS lost it.
- AC_OPENMP compiles its probe with LDFLAGS; -fopenmp there (conda builds
  set it) reads as "none needed", but the object compiles never see
  LDFLAGS, so the pragmas were dropped while libgomp was still linked.

Bioconda's trinity 2.15.2 builds 4-6 (May 2025 on) hit the second case:
ParaFly links libgomp but has no GOMP_ symbols, and Trinity's phase 2
runs one component at a time whatever --CPU says. Configure now probes
without LDFLAGS and quotes the substitution; configure regenerated with
autoreconf -fi.
